<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">European Free Trade Association</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1960">1960</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as EFTA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The European Free Trade Association is a free-trade organisation founded in 1960 by seven European states outside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a>. Most founders later joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>, and its members are now Iceland, Liechtenstein, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, the first three of which belong to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-area">European Economic Area</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/european-free-trade-association.jpg" alt="European Free Trade Association" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EFTA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EFTA_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
